  (text "1:1 divider - both resistors MUST be equal" (at 300.99 205.74 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "6f3d38c4-0d58-47e7-a79a-a485aaa3541f"))
  (rectangle (start 25.4 207.01) (end 277.4 276.86) (stroke (width 0.1) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "27d00f5c-472b-42c9-888f-c69a8144f24d"))
  (text "ASSEMBLY NOTES" (at 29.21 214.63 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) bold) (justify left)) (uuid "61a6c3d2-c8bd-436f-9e32-ff4284cbd63c"))
  (text "1. All GPIO numbers are read directly from firmware v4.7.5-OLED by the generator script;" (at 29.21 220.98 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left)) (uuid "40b9b28a-e193-4ed0-8e62-7069ec331c18"))
  (text "   they are never typed in by hand. Re-run tools/kicad-gen/gen_schematics.py after a pin change." (at 29.21 227.33 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left)) (uuid "9914ea1c-473e-495f-a426-c0dd568ea37e"))
  (text "2. Both buttons use pinMode(INPUT_PULLUP), so they wire straight to GND. No external pull-ups." (at 29.21 233.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left)) (uuid "f36aad1a-672d-48f1-9293-15d11b1e2beb"))
  (text "3. SW1 MUST sit on an RTC GPIO (0-21): it wakes the board from deep sleep via ext0 at logic level 0." (at 29.21 240.03 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left)) (uuid "7f72eced-c50e-422c-9acd-ef7b0cb0a281"))
  (text "4. Most OLED breakout modules already carry the I2C pull-ups. If yours does not," (at 29.21 246.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left)) (uuid "d78a2bf5-e0cb-4082-9abf-2415815959d9"))
  (text "   add 4.7k from SDA to 3V3 and 4.7k from SCL to 3V3." (at 29.21 252.73 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left)) (uuid "7a1c885a-72f8-40a5-a2b3-c238af5c4721"))
  (text "5. The I2C bus runs at 400 kHz per the SH1106 datasheet. Keep both wires as short as practical." (at 29.21 259.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left)) (uuid "98afcbec-4d28-458a-9cd3-f4f7c09f89d9"))
  (text "6. R1 and R2 must be equal. The firmware computes (raw/4095) x 3.3 x 2.0, which fixes the ratio at 1:1." (at 29.21 265.43 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left)) (uuid "92ca14e4-ea68-453a-8bde-96d08868f12a"))
  (text "7. A full 4.2V cell divides down to 2.1V, comfortably inside the ESP32-S3 ADC input range." (at 29.21 271.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left)) (uuid "d9e79e21-f194-4d63-a2b7-20e8482e9696"))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
